.el .ds Aq '
.TH SCMD 1  "scmd 0.3.0" SupremeCommander
.SH NAME
scmd \- SupremeCommander — orthodox file manager for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscmd\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-plugins\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-keymap\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-themes\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-commands\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-languages\fR] [\fB\-\-check\-keymap\fR] [\fB\-\-export\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-dump\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-paths\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-plugins\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
SupremeCommander is a two\-panel file manager for the terminal that works the same way on Linux, macOS and Windows: one program, one set of keys, one configuration file.
.PP
Two panels side by side, the function keys along the bottom saying what they do right now, and a command line underneath. Copying, moving and deleting run as jobs with progress and a way to stop them. Archives open as directories. The viewer streams a file of any size and disassembles a binary; the editor edits lines or bytes. SFTP panels are panels like any other.
.PP
The keys are FAR\*(Aqs by default, with a Midnight Commander profile; every action is a named command and every command can be bound to a key. Press F1 inside the program for the manual, whose key and command chapters are generated from the keymap in force.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Use this configuration file instead of the default one
.TP
\fB\-\-plugins\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Use this plugins directory (the only directory sc ever reads besides the config file)
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Theme id (commander, black, white, matrix, tron, blade, or an external one)
.TP
\fB\-\-keymap\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Keymap profile: a built\-in one (far, mc) or a [[keymap]] block from the config file
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Interface language: en, it, de, fr, es, ru, zh, or auto
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<KEY=VALUE>\fR
Override a setting, e.g. \-\-set panel.show_hidden=true
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-themes\fR
List the themes found in this run and where each came from
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-commands\fR
List every command id (the vocabulary keys, menus and plugins bind to)
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-languages\fR
List the interface languages compiled in
.TP
\fB\-\-check\-keymap\fR
Validate the keymap and print the resolved bindings
.TP
\fB\-\-export\-theme\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Print a theme as TOML, to start an external theme from
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-config\fR
Print the effective configuration
.TP
\fB\-\-paths\fR
Print where the config file, the state file and the plugins directory are
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-plugins\fR
List the plugins found in the plugins directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Directory for the left panel, and optionally for the right one
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/scmd/config.toml
The settings. B\-\-dump\-configR prints the effective ones. On macOS this is under
.I ~/Library/Application Support/scmd
and on Windows under
.I %APPDATA%\scmd .
.TP
.I ~/.config/scmd/keymap.toml
Your own key bindings, applied over the profile named by B\-\-keymapR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scmd/session.toml
Where the panels were when the program last exited.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scmd/themes/
Colour schemes. A TOML file dropped in here is found at startup; B\-\-export\-themeR
prints a built-in one to start from.
.TP
.I ~/.config/scmd/sites.toml
Stored connections: the host, the user and the path, never a password.
.SH KEYS
.B F1
help,
.B F3
view,
.B F4
edit,
.B F5
copy,
.B F6
move or rename,
.B F7
make a directory,
.B F8
delete,
.B F9
the menu bar,
.B F10
leave,
.B F12
the screens.
.B Tab
moves between the panels and
.B Insert
selects.
.PP
A panel holds more than one directory at a time:
.B Ctrl+Alt+T
opens another tab,
.B Ctrl+Alt+N
and
.B Ctrl+Alt+P
step along the row,
.B Ctrl+Alt+W
closes one,
.B Ctrl+Alt+M
hands it to the other panel and
.B Ctrl+Alt+K
locks it to its directory.
.PP
Folders are kept to hand on ten digits:
.B Ctrl+Shift+0..9
sets one,
.B Alt+0..9
goes to it, and
.B Ctrl+D
opens the whole list.
.PP
Those are the defaults of the
.B far
profile; the
.B mc
profile is Midnight Commander's. Every action is a named command,
.B \-\-list\-commands
prints them all, and
.B \-\-check\-keymap
says whether a keymap is sound. The help inside the program (BF1R) generates its key and
command chapters from the keymap actually in force, so it cannot drift.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Normal exit, including every informational option above.
.TP
1
The configuration, the keymap or an argument could not be used; the reason is on standard
error.
